{"id":26972,"date":"2025-04-24T12:26:58","date_gmt":"2025-04-24T16:26:58","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/biolongevitylabs.com\/?post_type=product&#038;p=26972"},"modified":"2026-08-17T15:58:01","modified_gmt":"2026-08-17T19:58:01","slug":"thymagen-20mg","status":"publish","type":"product","link":"https:\/\/biolongevitylabs.com\/product\/thymagen-20mg\/","title":{"rendered":"Thymagen (Thymogen) (20mg)"},"content":{"rendered":"<h2>Thymagen (Thymogen) Peptide Description<\/h2>\n<p class=\"whitespace-normal break-words\">Thymagen is a synthetic bioregulator peptide (Glu-Trp) originally isolated from thymalin, designed for laboratory research applications. This research-grade peptide enables in vitro studies of thymus-related immunity mechanisms, including T-cell differentiation and cyclic nucleotide balance.<\/p>\n<p class=\"whitespace-normal break-words\">Research demonstrates the effect of thymogen on cAMP and cGMP regulation through phosphodiesterase activity modulation in various models. Laboratory research applications include immunodeficiency studies and immune system regulation analysis. Research use only.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"whitespace-normal break-words\">Peptide Information<\/h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Property<\/th>\n<th>Value<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Peptide Sequence<\/td>\n<td>H-Glu-Trp-OH<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Molecular Formula<\/td>\n<td>C\u2081\u2086H\u2081\u2089N\u2083O\u2085<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Molecular Weight<\/td>\n<td>333.34 g\/mol<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CAS Number<\/td>\n<td>38101-59-6<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PubChem CID<\/td>\n<td>100094<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Research-grade Thymagen dipeptide bioregulator for laboratory studies of thymus function and immune cell differentiation.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"featured_media":27264,"template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"site-sidebar-layout":"default","site-content-layout":"","ast-site-content-layout":